# A file written under an explicit `L2:` holds the same record as an .lm2 file the builder wraps (the book #scope: «Код L2
# пишется под ресивером `L2:`; его запись лежит в графе как записана ... Файл `.lm2` сам по себе как обёрнут в этот
# ресивер»): the record L2 is the one field of the file and the dump prints it as written; the run passes through it to its
# content (plan #one-graph-plan, L1), so the write through the explicit path takes place. Before L1 the block was a named
# data Structure and its code did not run (the run answered 3, seen stayed 0).
L2:
    (
        Observed:
            int: seen 0
    )
    fn: two () int
        return: 2
    int: base 3
    shared\Observed\seen := base - two()
